2026-07-20T02:50:37.3771290Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3771555Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3772014Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3772375Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3772573Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3772812Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3773013Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3773235Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3773434Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3773689Z         def inc(x):
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3773895Z             return x + 1
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3774106Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3774282Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3774479Z         def test_answer():
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3774720Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3774946Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3775119Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3775310Z     To execute it::
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3775507Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3775689Z         $ pytest
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3775972Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3776411Z         collected 1 items
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3776629Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3776819Z         test_sample.py F
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3777041Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3777280Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3777677Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3778020Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3778222Z             def test_answer():
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3778482Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3778735Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3779068Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3779310Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3779509Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3779844Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3780151Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3780329Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3781190Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3782036Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3782208Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3782382Z     Features
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3782581Z     --------
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3782767Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3783280Z     - Detailed info on failing `assert statements <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html>`_ (no need to remember ``self.assert*`` names)
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3783857Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3784051Z     - `Auto-discovery
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3784453Z       <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#python-test-discovery>`_
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3784895Z       of test modules and functions
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3785142Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3785474Z     - `Modular fixtures <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/fixtures.html>`_ for
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3785956Z       managing small or parametrized long-lived test resources
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3786271Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3786599Z     - Can run `unittest <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/unittest.html>`_ (or trial)
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3787016Z       test suites out of the box
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3787252Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3787446Z     - Python 3.10+ or PyPy3
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3787673Z     
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3788191Z     - Rich plugin architecture, with over 1300+ `external plugins <https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/plugin_list.html>`_ and thriving community
2026-07-20T02:50:37.3788772Z     
